 ## Verified Facts
 
 - `TripViewBeta.loadAndPresent` accepts `HybridIdentifier`, forwarding UUID or folio lookups through `getTrip` and constructing the detail from the returned response. Trip-list and followup selections pass `.id(item.id)`; status callbacks continue to use the loaded trip's concrete UUID.
+- `TripViewBeta` shows an Estatus metric immediately before Creado in its top summary, using the shared Spanish status descriptions and existing metric styling. Its persistent value element binds to the existing status state, updating after API success and server refresh; the summary grid explicitly provides one account column and five metric columns. Browser rendering remains unverified.
 - `TripViewBeta` reserves a 35px status action row below its right-side data grid. Pending trips expose Iniciar Viaje and Cancelar Viaje; in-progress trips expose Completar Viaje and Cancelar Viaje; terminal states expose neither. Start/complete actions use the shared green crystal modifier and cancel uses red, with matching hover/focus accents and a dimmed disabled state. `ConfirmTripStatusUpdate` gathers the typed transition, a trimmed comment (required for cancellation), and `ChangeTripStatusMedia` grouped by fiscal merchandise item ID. Its source uses the existing unregistered `.asset` image-upload/camera pipeline with per-file XHR progress/status checks. Camera requests use `eventid: nil` and `multipleTakes: true`, with no request-time upload placeholder or camera-pending controls. New selected/initiate capture IDs attach to the most recently requested merchandise row; IDs already assigned keep their original row and terminal IDs cannot be revived by duplicate or delayed events. Confirmation remains available and snapshots only completed images; each row retains its numbered completed-file count, first completed image avatar and existing MediaViewer gallery. Removal aborts pending local uploads and ignores late responses. Before presentation/submission, asset merchandise requires unique linked store/warehouse/subaccount origin and destination snapshots; media requires unique trip-merchandise IDs and safe image basenames. The server remains authoritative for actual asset state and tenant records. The beta `changeStatus` method submits the trip ID, requested status, comment and media through the typed wrapper. Status actions are disabled while the request is pending. Only a successful API response changes the local trip/status and calls the parent status callback; a guarded getTrip refresh loads the new status/comment notes, while failed requests retain the prior status. Responses from a changed session are ignored, while successful responses still notify the parent if the detail was closed. These facts were verified in source; browser/upload behavior remains unverified.
 - `MediaViewer` honors `currentView` with a zero-index fallback, presents clickable `thump_` thumbnails and previous/next navigation for multiple files, and uses the selected file for downloads/rotations/deletion. Direct image source assignment avoids an older image-load callback replacing a newer selection. Each `MediaFile` can supply its own URL base; `allowsMediaActions: false` hides mutation/download actions for staged evidence while existing callers retain the default behavior.
 - `Sources/App/App.swift` is the `@main` app entry point.
